B.MX=new A.h4("cn-03","Mosi-oa-Tunya: Nyami Nyami and the Smoke That Thunders","Victoria Falls / Zambezi River","Elder Simasiku (BaTonga River Guide)","Chidobe & Mukuni Traditional Ward","ChiTonga","3:50 min","Long before European cartographers drew their lines, our grandfathers worshipped the river dragon Nyami Nyami whose scales keep the Zambezi flowing and safeguard the fishing grounds.","Riverine ecology guardian folklore teaching sustainable fishing and water respect.",612,1224)
B.MY=new A.h4("cn-01","The Great Enclosure: Oral Songs of the Dry-Stone Builders","Great Zimbabwe UNESCO Monument (Masvingo)","Sekuru Munemo (Clan Custodian)","Morgenster & Nemamwa Elders Council","ChiShona","4:18 min","The granite stones were not placed by slaves or strangers. Our ancestors used the fire-and-water method to quarry granite blocks with precision without a drop of mortar. The walls breathe in harmony with the summer breezes.","A consecrated tribute to Mwari (The Creator) and ancestral guardian spirits of the Hungwe bird.",482.5,965)
B.MZ=new A.h4("cn-02","Njelele Shrine & The Rainmaking Ceremonies of Matobo","Matobo Sacred Granite Hills (Matabeleland)","Gogo Sibanda (Spiritual Keeper)","Dula & Silozwe Community Trust","SiNdebele","5:42 min","When the heat of October settles over the rocks, the elders walk barefoot into the inner caves of Njelele. No modern metals are carried. We ask for rain through the voice that echoes through the granite domes.","Sacred oracle shrine where national peace and agricultural abundance are prayed for.",394,788)
